    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.  The effect reads \"up to 4,\" therefore you can place any number from 1 to 4.",
        "question": "Can I use this card’s [On Play] [When Digivolving] effect to place just 2 cards in digivolution cards when I have 4 level 5 or lower [Argomon] in my trash?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  \"Lv.-\" Digimon don't have a level, therefore they can't be chosen as targets for an effect that deletes up to 4 levels' worth of Digimon.",
        "question": "When I use this card's [On Play] [When Digivolving] effect to delete up to 4 levels' worth of Digimon, can I delete my opponent's \"Lv.-\" Digimon?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "If a card is removed from the trash before a triggered [On Deletion] effect activates, that [On Deletion] effect can't be activated.",
        "question": "BT17-048 [Argomon] was deleted while it had an [Argomon] with an [On Deletion] effect in its digivolution cards. I first used BT17-048 [Argomon]'s [On Deletion] effect to play this card. At such times, if I use this card's [On Play] effect to place [Argomon] in digivolution cards before activating the [On Deletion] effect, what happens to that effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
